WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:08.400
By 2030, the world’s data centers are expected to use more than double the electricity they use today.
预计到2030年，全球数据中心的用电量将达到现在的两倍多。

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:10.680
AI is the main driver.
人工智能是主要推动因素。

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:15.250
It forces countries to look for new ways to solve the big problem.
它迫使各国寻找新办法，来解决这个大难题。

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:20.990
China is leading the way by putting data centers under the sea as a greener solution.
中国把数据中心放到海底，以此作为一种更环保的解决办法，在这方面走在了前列。

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:27.600
In December 2022, Hainan became home to China’s first underwater data center.
2022年12月，中国第一个海底数据中心落户海南。

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:32.780
This was followed by a more advanced project in Shanghai in 2025.
随后，2025年，上海又有了一个更先进的项目。

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:37.890
AI servers give off heat while working, making the temperature rise.
人工智能服务器工作时会散发热量，使温度升高。

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:44.060
If the heat isn’t taken away in time, the servers won’t run well and may even break down.
如果不及时把热量带走，服务器就会运行不好，甚至可能出故障。

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:51.430
On-land data centers have to use up to 40% of their electricity just for cooling AI servers.
陆上数据中心光是为人工智能服务器降温，就不得不用掉多达40%的电力。

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:57.540
Underwater data centers, like the one in Shanghai, use pipes to pump seawater.
海底数据中心，比如上海的那座，用管道来输送海水。

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:01.620
Seawater goes through the radiators on the back of the servers.
海水流经服务器背面的散热器。

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:04.560
It takes in heat and carries it away.
它吸收热量，并把热量带走。

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:10.150
The sea temperature is about 15°C, perfect for natural cooling.
海水温度约为15°C，非常适合自然冷却。

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:13.560
In this way, electricity is saved.
这样一来，就节省了电力。

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:27.270
An assessment from the China Academy of Information and Communications Technology shows the underwater data center uses at least 30% less electricity than on-land data centers thanks to natural cooling.
中国信息通信研究院的一项评估显示，得益于自然冷却，海底数据中心的用电量比陆上数据中心至少低30%。

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:32.340
Underwater data centers can also reduce land usage by 80%.
海底数据中心还能把土地使用量减少80%。

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:42.750
And the one in Shanghai offers another benefit: it will get more than 95% of its electricity from a kind of renewable energy—wind energy.
而且上海的那座还有另一个好处：它将有超过95%的电力来自一种可再生能源——风能。

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:47.960
And the use of tidal and wave energy is also taken into consideration.
此外，利用潮汐能和波浪能也在考虑之中。

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:55.580
China’s efforts in developing underwater data centers show its promise to create low-carbon digital infrastructure.
中国为发展海底数据中心所做的努力，体现了其建设低碳数字基础设施的承诺。

00:01:56.380 --> 00:02:04.790
The move not only helps reduce the environmental impact of AI, but also could set a new standard for sustainable computing worldwide.
这一举措不仅有助于减少人工智能对环境的影响，还可能在全球范围内为可持续算力树立新标准。
